
<%# ============================================================================
RESEARCH COLLECTION INTELLIGENCE — FIELD MANUAL

Purpose:
Provide a beginner-friendly, encyclopedia-level explanation of the research
intelligence model, including questions, objectives, findings, evidence,
contradictions, synthesis, milestones, signals, and relationships.

Usage:
  <%= render "admin/ecosystems/load_sources/entities/research_collections/research_collection_intelligence/field_manual" %>

Notes:
- Presentation-only partial; it does not modify research data.
- Uses Tailwind utility classes and semantic HTML.
============================================================================ %>

<section
  aria-labelledby="research-field-manual-title"
  class="relative mb-10 overflow-hidden rounded-[32px] border-2 border-violet-100 bg-gradient-to-b from-white via-violet-50/30 to-slate-50 shadow-md shadow-violet-100/40"
>
  <%# Decorative background %>
  <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 overflow-hidden" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="absolute -right-24 -top-24 h-72 w-72 rounded-full bg-violet-200/30 blur-3xl"></div>
    <div class="absolute -bottom-24 -left-24 h-72 w-72 rounded-full bg-orange-200/25 blur-3xl"></div>
    <div class="absolute right-20 top-20 h-24 w-24 rounded-full border-2 border-violet-100/70"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="relative z-10 p-5 sm:p-8 lg:p-10">

    <%# Header labels %>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-violet-200 bg-violet-50 px-4 py-2 text-[11px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-violet-700">
        <span class="h-2 w-2 animate-pulse rounded-full bg-violet-500"></span>
        Research field manual
      </span>

      <span class="rounded-full border border-orange-200 bg-orange-50 px-4 py-2 text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-orange-700">
        Knowledge protocol 01
      </span>
    </div>

    <%# Hero %>
    <div class="mt-7 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-center">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <div class="text-[12px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-violet-500">
          Research architecture
        </div>

        <h2 id="research-field-manual-title" class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-3xl font-black leading-tight tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
          How does research intelligence actually work?
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:text-[17px]">
          Research intelligence is the organized interpretation of a research
          collection. It brings together questions, goals, observations,
          findings, supporting material, and unresolved disagreements so that
          a researcher can understand not only what has been recorded, but
          also what remains uncertain and what deserves attention next.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
          An individual record represents one piece of the investigation.
          The collection provides the broader context in which those records
          can be compared, connected, challenged, and synthesized.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border-2 border-amber-100 bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-50 via-white to-orange-50/60 p-5 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-100 text-xl">
              💡
            </div>

            <div>
              <div class="text-[12px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-700">
                Beginner rule
              </div>

              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 sm:text-[15px]">
                <strong class="text-slate-800">A recorded finding is a claim to evaluate, not automatically a proven fact.</strong>
                Always ask what supports it, how strong that support is,
                whether credible sources disagree, and what limitations remain.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Visual concept card %>
      <div class="relative lg:col-span-5">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-sm rounded-[28px] border-2 border-indigo-100 bg-white p-6 shadow-lg shadow-indigo-100/60 transition duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1">
          <div class="flex h-20 w-20 items-center justify-center rounded-[24px] border-2 border-indigo-200 bg-gradient-to-br from-indigo-500 to-violet-500 text-4xl shadow-lg shadow-indigo-200/70">
            🧠
          </div>

          <div class="mt-6 text-[11px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-indigo-500">
            Research collection
          </div>

          <h3 class="mt-1 text-xl font-black text-slate-900">
            A connected knowledge system
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
            Multiple records become more useful when their meaning,
            evidence, status, and relationships can be examined together.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-6 space-y-3">
            <% [
                 ["Questions", "Identify uncertainty", "border-orange-100 bg-orange-50 text-orange-700"],
                 ["Findings", "Describe emerging results", "border-violet-100 bg-violet-50 text-violet-700"],
                 ["Evidence", "Support or challenge claims", "border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-700"],
                 ["Synthesis", "Explain the overall picture", "border-sky-100 bg-sky-50 text-sky-700"]
               ].each do |label, description, classes| %>
              <div class="rounded-xl border p-3 <%= classes %>">
                <div class="text-xs font-black"><%= label %></div>
                <div class="mt-1 text-xs leading-5 opacity-80"><%= description %></div>
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Architecture map %>
    <div class="mt-12">
      <div class="text-[12px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-400">
        System map
      </div>

      <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-black text-slate-800">
        From an unknown to a defensible conclusion
      </h3>

      <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
        This is a conceptual workflow, not a guarantee that every investigation
        follows a strictly linear sequence. Research commonly returns to earlier
        stages when new evidence changes the questions or assumptions.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4">
        <% [
             {
               icon: "❓",
               title: "1. Question",
               description: "Define what is unknown, disputed, or in need of explanation.",
               example: "What causes the observed change?",
               classes: "border-orange-100 bg-orange-50/70 text-orange-700"
             },
             {
               icon: "🎯",
               title: "2. Objective",
               description: "Turn the question into a practical investigative goal.",
               example: "Compare possible explanations.",
               classes: "border-sky-100 bg-sky-50/70 text-sky-700"
             },
             {
               icon: "🔬",
               title: "3. Finding",
               description: "Record a result or claim derived from the investigation.",
               example: "Several sources report a similar pattern.",
               classes: "border-violet-100 bg-violet-50/70 text-violet-700"
             },
             {
               icon: "📚",
               title: "4. Evidence",
               description: "Evaluate the material that supports or challenges the claim.",
               example: "Check source quality and methodology.",
               classes: "border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/70 text-emerald-700"
             }
           ].each do |stage| %>
          <article class="rounded-2xl border-2 p-5 shadow-sm transition duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-md <%= stage[:classes] %>">
            <div class="text-2xl"><%= stage[:icon] %></div>
            <h4 class="mt-4 text-sm font-black"><%= stage[:title] %></h4>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600"><%= stage[:description] %></p>
            <div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-white/80 bg-white/80 p-3">
              <div class="text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-400">Example</div>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-600"><%= stage[:example] %></p>
            </div>
          </article>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4 rounded-2xl border-2 border-indigo-100 bg-indigo-50/60 p-5">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="text-2xl">🔄</span>
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-sm font-black text-indigo-800">5. Synthesize, challenge, and revise</h4>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
              Compare findings across the collection, identify contradictions,
              document limitations, and determine whether the original question
              has been answered. If important gaps remain, refine the objectives
              or gather additional evidence and repeat the cycle.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Encyclopedia glossary %>
    <div class="mt-12">
      <div class="text-[12px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-400">
        Encyclopedia glossary
      </div>

      <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-black text-slate-800">
        Understand every research component
      </h3>

      <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
        Each component answers a different question. Keeping these roles distinct
        prevents progress indicators from being confused with evidence quality
        or conclusions from being confused with raw observations.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <% [
             {
               icon: "❓",
               title: "Research questions",
               question: "What do we need to know?",
               explanation: "Questions define the uncertainty that motivates the investigation. An unresolved question is not necessarily a failure; it may identify an important knowledge gap, a missing source, or a question that cannot yet be answered confidently.",
               example: "Which factors are associated with the observed outcome?",
               classes: "border-orange-100 bg-orange-50/30"
             },
             {
               icon: "🎯",
               title: "Objectives",
               question: "What work will address the question?",
               explanation: "Objectives translate broad questions into actionable goals. Useful objectives are specific enough to guide research activities and assess whether a task has been completed. Completing an objective does not automatically mean the hypothesis was confirmed.",
               example: "Compare the methods and results of three independent studies.",
               classes: "border-sky-100 bg-sky-50/30"
             },
             {
               icon: "🔬",
               title: "Findings",
               question: "What did the investigation discover?",
               explanation: "A finding is a recorded research result, observation, or claim. Its interpretation depends on context, methodology, source quality, and the evidence attached to it. Findings can be preliminary, contested, or later revised.",
               example: "Two studies observed a similar association.",
               classes: "border-violet-100 bg-violet-50/30"
             },
             {
               icon: "📚",
               title: "Evidence",
               question: "What supports or challenges a claim?",
               explanation: "Evidence is the source material used to assess a finding. It may include documents, measurements, datasets, experiments, interviews, or other records. Evidence should be relevant to the claim and evaluated for reliability, provenance, limitations, and potential bias.",
               example: "A dataset and its documented collection method.",
               classes: "border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/30"
             },
             {
               icon: "⚡",
               title: "Contradictions",
               question: "Where do claims appear to disagree?",
               explanation: "A contradiction indicates a possible conflict between claims or findings. The disagreement may result from different definitions, samples, time periods, methods, assumptions, or genuine incompatibility. A detected contradiction is a prompt to investigate, not proof that either source is wrong.",
               example: "Two studies report different effects under different conditions.",
               classes: "border-rose-100 bg-rose-50/30"
             },
             {
               icon: "📝",
               title: "Research synthesis",
               question: "What does the combined evidence suggest?",
               explanation: "Synthesis integrates information from multiple findings into a coherent interpretation. It distinguishes direct observations from interpretations and conclusions, identifies recurring patterns, and records uncertainty instead of hiding disagreements.",
               example: "The effect appears in one population but remains uncertain in another.",
               classes: "border-amber-100 bg-amber-50/30"
             },
             {
               icon: "🏁",
               title: "Milestones",
               question: "What deliverables have been completed?",
               explanation: "Milestones track planned stages or deliverables. They are useful for project management, but a completed milestone measures recorded progress rather than the validity of the research result.",
               example: "Complete source collection and document the methodology.",
               classes: "border-fuchsia-100 bg-fuchsia-50/30"
             },
             {
               icon: "🕸️",
               title: "Relationships",
               question: "How are research elements connected?",
               explanation: "Relationships record meaningful connections among research records. Depending on the relationship type, a connection might indicate support, dependency, shared context, derivation, disagreement, or another domain-specific link.",
               example: "A finding is supported by a particular evidence record.",
               classes: "border-indigo-100 bg-indigo-50/30"
             }
           ].each do |item| %>
          <article class="rounded-2xl border-2 p-5 shadow-sm <%= item[:classes] %>">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <div class="flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl border border-white bg-white text-xl shadow-sm">
                <%= item[:icon] %>
              </div>
              <div class="min-w-0">
                <h4 class="text-sm font-black text-slate-800"><%= item[:title] %></h4>
                <p class="mt-1 text-xs font-bold text-slate-500"><%= item[:question] %></p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600"><%= item[:explanation] %></p>

            <div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-white bg-white/80 p-3">
              <div class="text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-400">Illustrative example</div>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-600"><%= item[:example] %></p>
            </div>
          </article>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Understanding confidence %>
    <div class="mt-12 rounded-[26px] border-2 border-emerald-100 bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-50/80 via-white to-sky-50/50 p-5 md:p-7">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <div class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-100 text-xl">
          ⚖️
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-800">
            How to interpret confidence and evidence quality
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
            Confidence labels summarize an assessment of a finding. Their meaning
            depends on how your application defines and assigns them. Unless the
            underlying rules explicitly say otherwise, a high-confidence label
            should not be treated as a statistical probability or a guarantee of truth.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 bg-white p-4">
          <div class="text-xs font-black text-emerald-700">High confidence</div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">
            A strong assessment within the system's criteria. Still inspect the
            underlying evidence, assumptions, and possible limitations.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-white p-4">
          <div class="text-xs font-black text-amber-700">Medium confidence</div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">
            Some support exists, but uncertainty, incomplete coverage, or
            unresolved alternatives may remain.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
          <div class="text-xs font-black text-slate-700">Low confidence</div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">
            Treat the finding cautiously. Further verification or better
            evidence may be needed before relying on it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-4">
        <p class="text-xs leading-5 text-amber-900/80">
          <strong>Remember:</strong> the number of evidence records is not the
          same as the strength of evidence. Many records may repeat the same
          original source, use weak methods, or fail to address the claim being
          evaluated.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Metric interpretation %>
    <div class="mt-12">
      <div class="text-[12px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-400">
        Metric interpretation
      </div>

      <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-black text-slate-800">
        What the dashboard numbers do — and do not — tell you
      </h3>

      <div class="mt-5 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border-2 border-slate-100 bg-white">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 divide-y divide-slate-100 md:grid-cols-2 md:divide-x md:divide-y-0">
          <div class="p-5">
            <h4 class="text-sm font-black text-slate-800">Questions resolved</h4>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
              Indicates how many questions are recorded as resolved compared
              with the total. Check whether the answer is documented and
              supported before treating resolution as conclusive.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5">
            <h4 class="text-sm font-black text-slate-800">Objective progress</h4>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
              Describes recorded objective completion. It does not directly
              measure the originality, accuracy, or significance of the result.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-t border-slate-100 p-5">
            <h4 class="text-sm font-black text-slate-800">Finding confidence</h4>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
              Shows the current confidence categories assigned to findings.
              Interpret them according to the application's assessment rules.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-t border-slate-100 p-5">
            <h4 class="text-sm font-black text-slate-800">Evidence coverage</h4>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
              Indicates how widely evidence is represented across workspaces.
              Coverage alone does not establish that the evidence is sufficient
              or relevant to every claim.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-t border-slate-100 p-5">
            <h4 class="text-sm font-black text-slate-800">Contradiction count</h4>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
              Shows the conflicts currently detected or recorded. More
              contradictions may reflect more thorough investigation rather
              than worse research.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-t border-slate-100 p-5">
            <h4 class="text-sm font-black text-slate-800">Relationship count</h4>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
              Shows recorded connections between research elements. A larger
              network is useful only when its connections have meaningful,
              interpretable semantics.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Practical examples %>
    <div class="mt-12">
      <div class="text-[12px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-400">
        Practical applications
      </div>

      <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-indigo-100 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-md">
          <div class="text-2xl">📖</div>
          <h4 class="mt-4 text-sm font-black text-slate-800">Encyclopedia building</h4>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
            Combine facts, source references, disagreements, and cross-links
            to build entries that preserve context instead of presenting
            isolated claims.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 text-[11px] font-black text-indigo-600">Connect knowledge</div>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-violet-100 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-md">
          <div class="text-2xl">🧪</div>
          <h4 class="mt-4 text-sm font-black text-slate-800">Scientific investigation</h4>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
            Track research questions, compare methods, record results, inspect
            inconsistent outcomes, and make limitations visible in the final
            synthesis.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 text-[11px] font-black text-violet-600">Evaluate claims</div>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-emerald-100 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-md">
          <div class="text-2xl">🌐</div>
          <h4 class="mt-4 text-sm font-black text-slate-800">Knowledge operations</h4>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
            Coordinate multiple workspaces, monitor evidence distribution,
            identify missing connections, and determine which investigative
            tasks need attention.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 text-[11px] font-black text-emerald-600">Improve coverage</div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Workflow and mission %>
    <div class="mt-12 rounded-[26px] border-2 border-orange-100 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-50/70 via-white to-emerald-50/50 p-5 md:p-7">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-5 sm:flex-row sm:items-start">
        <div class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl border border-orange-200 bg-orange-100 text-xl">
          🎯
        </div>

        <div class="min-w-0">
          <div class="text-[12px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-orange-600">
            Your research mission
          </div>

          <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-black text-slate-800">
            Turn recorded information into a traceable explanation
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
            Start with the unresolved questions. Check which objectives address
            them, inspect the findings produced, and follow each important claim
            back to its evidence. Investigate contradictions, document
            limitations, and use synthesis to explain what the combined
            information supports — and what it cannot yet establish.
          </p>

          <ol class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <% [
                 ["01", "Review open questions", "Identify the most important unknowns."],
                 ["02", "Check objectives", "Confirm that work addresses the questions."],
                 ["03", "Trace evidence", "Inspect sources and their limitations."],
                 ["04", "Resolve conflicts", "Compare competing explanations fairly."],
                 ["05", "Write synthesis", "Separate observations from conclusions."],
                 ["06", "Refresh intelligence", "Recalculate the dashboard after updates."]
               ].each do |number, title, description| %>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border border-white bg-white/80 p-3">
                <span class="flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-orange-100 bg-orange-50 text-[10px] font-black text-orange-700">
                  <%= number %>
                </span>
                <div>
                  <div class="text-xs font-black text-slate-800"><%= title %></div>
                  <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500"><%= description %></p>
                </div>
              </li>
            <% end %>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Closing principle %>
    <div class="mt-8 border-t-2 border-slate-100 pt-5">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
        <div class="font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-400">
          RESEARCH_PROTOCOL :: EVIDENCE :: SYNTHESIS
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-600">
          <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span>
          Field manual available
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">
        The goal is not to eliminate all uncertainty. The goal is to make
        uncertainty visible, explain the basis for each important claim,
        preserve competing interpretations, and show how the research
        supports its conclusions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>